results/arc3_trm_verifier_rerank.json (n=31-task subset of TRM arc_v1 candidates). Reused the
TRM evaluator's exact de-aug/voting on the dumped per-augmentation predictions, then reranked
TRM's candidates with the Carnot union_max invariant ensemble vs TRM's own frequency vote.

RESULT (honest, FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK-disciplined): the verifier does NOT beat TRM's vote.
  TRM_VOTE pass@2 = 0.484 (best)   oracle pass@1000 = 0.613 (~13pp present-but-mis-voted headroom)
  VERIFIER pass@2 = 0.484 (pass@1 LOWER 0.387; 16 top-1 flips, net -1)
  HYBRID   pass@2 = 0.452 (hurt)
  captured of the headroom: 0.0
This matches the design survey's expectation: TRM's mis-votes are structurally valid and sit in
the hand-invariants' null space; TRM's augmentation-frequency vote is already a strong selector.

THE VALUE (operator directive — missing verifiers are the product): the gap census on the 5
uncaptured tasks (correct in TRM's pool, verifier still missed) confirms ALL THREE seeded gaps on
REAL mis-votes (not synthetic distractors): GAP-1 transpose/orientation 2, GAP-2 variable-dim 1,
GAP-3 content-in-null-space 2. ops/verifier_gaps.md updated with this empirical confirmation +
a model-native-from-TRM-activations ALT design (arXiv:2604.17614) as the GAP-3 follow-up.

Caveat: 31-task subset; counts small but directional. Re-confirm at scale.

